## Remote client (2026-10-12)

A native visionOS and iPadOS client that browses the sessions and
working sets of several running Switchboard installations and sends
prompts to them is specified in `docs/remote-client.md`: a port over
the control port's wire contract, pairing with a pinned host key, one
revision counter and `changed` events, and content work off the frame
thread. The plan is Spike 22 and then Milestone A as five commits.

Built so far:

- **A0, the conversation cache in the app.** Parsed transcripts moved
  from `UiState` to `SwitchboardApp::conversations`
  (`content::ConversationCache`): each entry keeps the handle and file
  time it was read through, `is_current` answers the refresh without a
  read, and the views reach the cache through `DrawCtx::conversations`.
  A seeded conversation (tests, the script) has no handle and no file
  time and is never read over. Behaviour is unchanged; the UI tests
  seed the new place.
---219
  project or the Dispatch runner is granted sets, and
  `switchboard-env exec -- <command>` puts their variables in that one
  child's environment, resolved over `env.resolve`.

### Trust boundary

Switchboard executes commands from records, so where records come from
matters. A record that arrived via `git clone` or a branch checkout must
never run anything on its own.

- **Milestone 1: private state only.** Records live under Application
---ALLOW
fn the_allowlist_refuses_everything_else_with_no_side_effect() {
    let mut port = port();
    let (_, project, session) = seed(&mut port, "");
    let token = pair(&mut port, "ABCD2345", Scope::Control, "Pad");
    let t = Some(token.as_str());
    for (method, path) in [
        ("POST", format!("/api/v1/sessions/{session}/kill")),
        ("POST", format!("/api/v1/sessions/{session}/notes")),
        ("GET", format!("/api/v1/sessions/{session}/env")),
        ("GET", "/api/v1/env/resolve".into()),
        ("POST", "/api/v1/projects".into()),
        ("DELETE", format!("/api/v1/sessions/{session}")),
        ("GET", "/api/v2/projects".into()),
    ] {
        let (status, reply) = call(&mut port, method, &path, t, r#"{"text":"hi"}"#);
        assert_eq!(
            (status, code(&reply)),
            (404, "not_found"),
            "{method} {path}: {reply}"
---HTTP
fn http(
    addr: SocketAddr,
    config: &Arc<ClientConfig>,
    method: &str,
    path: &str,
    bearer: Option<&str>,
    body: &str,
) -> std::io::Result<(u16, String)> {
    let tcp = TcpStream::connect(addr)?;
    tcp.set_read_timeout(Some(Duration::from_secs(10)))?;
    let conn = ClientConnection::new(
        Arc::clone(config),
        ServerName::try_from("localhost").unwrap(),
    )
    .map_err(std::io::Error::other)?;
    let mut s = StreamOwned::new(conn, tcp);
    while s.conn.is_handshaking() {
        s.conn.complete_io(&mut s.sock)?;
    }
    let auth = bearer
        .map(|t| format!("Authorization: Bearer {t}\r\n"))
        .unwrap_or_default();
    write!(
        s,
        "{method} {path} HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: localhost\r\n{auth}Content-Length: {}\r\n\r\n{body}",
        body.len()
    )?;
    s.flush()?;
    let mut reader = BufReader::new(s);
    let mut line = String::new();
    reader.read_line(&mut line)?;
    let status: u16 = line
        .split_whitespace()
        .nth(1)
        .and_then(|s| s.parse().ok())
        .ok_or_else(|| std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::InvalidData, line.clone()))?;
    let mut length = 0usize;
    loop {
        let mut h = String::new();
        reader.read_line(&mut h)?;
        let h = h.trim_end();
        if h.is_empty() {
            break;
        }
        if let Some(v) = h.strip_prefix("Content-Length:") {
            length = v.trim().parse().unwrap_or(0);
        }
    }
    let mut out = vec![0; length];
    reader.read_exact(&mut out)?;
    Ok((status, String::from_utf8_lossy(&out).into_owned()))
}

/// A request from a client thread, served by the app on this thread.
fn call(
    port: &mut Port,
---CERT
fn a_wrong_pin_fails_at_the_handshake_before_any_request() {
    let mut port = port();
    let other = pinned_client(&"00".repeat(32)).unwrap();
    let result = http(port.addr, &other, "GET", "/api/v1/info", None, "");
    assert!(result.is_err(), "{result:?}");
    // The right pin is still served.
    let (status, _) = get(&mut port, "/api/v1/info", None);
    assert_eq!(status, 200);
}

#[test]
fn pair_is_rate_limited_per_listener() {
    let mut port = port();
    let mut statuses = Vec::new();
    for _ in 0..7 {
        let (status, _) = call(&mut port, "POST", "/api/v1/pair", None, "{}");
        statuses.push(status);
    }
    assert_eq!(statuses, vec![403, 403, 403, 403, 403, 403, 429]);
    let (status, reply) = get(&mut port, "/api/v1/info", None);
    assert_eq!(status, 200, "info has its own limit: {reply}");
}

